SHELVED — the `mist` canvas background (14 Sep 2026)

A dark steel-teal / indigo / mauve variant of the living canvas, built off a
Calmora reference and then set aside ("i dont think we can use this"). None of
it is in the app. This file is the whole change as a git patch against
b08bec0; everything above the first `diff --git` line is ignored by git.

To look at it again:

    git apply .design/mist-canvas/mist-canvas.patch

(`git apply --check` first; the further main has moved, the likelier it needs
a 3-way apply: `git apply -3 ...`.)

What it did:
- a new `mist` variant in components/layout/CanvasShader.tsx, rendered on
  every route: twisted simplex folds, lighting from screen-space derivatives,
  pointer parallax on three layers, soft `#41818475` dashes
- light under the logo, easing dark once `data-entrance-hold` leaves <html>
  (hence the note added in LogoEntrance.tsx)
- nine `--color-canvas-mist-*` tokens on :root in app/globals.css
- figma-catchup § 9 and comment updates in Welcome.tsx and CheckScreen.tsx

Why it was not used, as measured:
- text on bare canvas fails contrast once dark: Welcome disclaimer 1.29:1,
  /check h1 2.07:1 and subtitle 1.28:1; an ink swap alone cannot fix it (the
  canvas spans ~97-178 of 255)
- the light-to-dark fade was never watched live (the preview pane was hidden)

