+## 9. The canvas's `mist` palette (14 Sep 2026)
+
+`CanvasShader`'s `mist` variant — now what every route renders — reads nine
+tokens declared on `:root` in `globals.css` that Figma does not have. It was
+asked for off a Calmora reference and reshaped through a day of direction on
+14 Sep 2026 ("no yellow", "give some darkness", "go darker and stay darker",
+"let the bottom go dark too", "tone up the colour, it's too monotone now",
+"use #41818475 instead of the peach"):
+
+| Token | Value | Role |
+| ----- | ----- | ---- |
+| `canvas/mist-1` · `-2` · `-3` | `#e0e9ec` · `#cddbe0` · `#c0d2d8` | the light ground, shown under the logo |
+| `canvas/mist-mauve` | `#d6c6cc` | the left-edge wash under the logo |
+| `canvas/mist-line` | `#41818475` | the soft diagonal dashes — ⚠️ the one token with an alpha, which the shader uses as their strength |
+| `canvas/mist-teal` | `#3e6570` | the shallow half of the shade |
+| `canvas/mist-indigo` | `#4f5878` | the deepest half of the shade |
+| `canvas/mist-glow` | `#8ec3cb` | cyan light on the faces turned to the light, and the sheen |
+| `canvas/mist-mauve-deep` | `#85728d` | the left-edge wash once it is dark |
+
+The ramp also reuses `gradient/canvas-end-desktop` and `-end-mobile`. The dark
+set lies far below the old `#acc5cc` floor, and **nothing clamps to it or keeps
+it off text**. **Add these as a canvas group if the treatment is approved**;
+the static `gradient/canvas-*` fallback is unchanged.
+
+⚠️ **KNOWN-FAILING UNDER `mist`, AND AWAITING A DECISION.** Measured on 14 Sep
+2026, after "let the bottom go dark too", by reading the canvas back and
+sweeping 300s of animation with the pointer in three places:
+
+| Text | Ink | Where | Worst |
+| ---- | --- | ----- | ----- |
+| Welcome disclaimer, after the logo | `text/secondary` | `/`, mobile (518) and 1440 | **1.29:1** |
+| Welcome disclaimer, before dusk falls | `text/secondary` | `/`, mobile (518) | **3.98:1** |
+| Hub subtitle ("Product compatibility") | `text/secondary` 14px | `/check`, mobile (518) | **1.28:1** |
+| Page `<h1>` ("Analysis") | `text/primary` 20px | `/check`, mobile (518) | **2.07:1** |
+
+The disclaimer passes through 3.36, 2.66 and 2.15:1 a quarter, half and three
+quarters of the way to dark, so not even the logo's light ground carries it to
+AA. "Mobile" is the preview pane's own phone-layout width, 518; nothing here
+was taken at the 440 frame width.
+
+The same inks sit on the same canvas everywhere else — the hub subtitles on
+`/check/no-profile`, `/progress`, `/progress/empty` and `/products`, and the
+empty-state and intro body on `/progress/empty`, `/check/no-profile`,
+`/investigation/profile` and `/investigation/analysis` — and fail the same way.
+The per-route figures taken earlier, at the first and much lighter shade, are
+superseded and were removed rather than left to read as current.
+
+⚠️ **AN INK SWAP ALONE WILL NOT CLOSE IT.** The canvas now spans roughly 97 to
+178 of 255 in brightness: dark ink fails on the shade, and white — estimated
+from the lightest pixel measured — would fail on the cyan light at about 2:1.
+Closing it needs text off bare canvas (a surface behind it), a narrower canvas
+range, or both.
